    "description": "Run the split critic for one round\n\n## Summary\n\nCrew's split critic now reviews a split once, the same way the spec critic does since the last change. Before, a blocking finding sent the split back for a fix and a new critic round, up to three times. Records show that a second round found a blocking problem in 1 report of 6, against 6 of 8 at round 1. Now the project lead fixes every accepted finding in the split itself, blocking ones included, logs each label and decline in one entry, and dispatches the work. A re-plan later in a run is a new split and gets its own one review.\n\n**Ticket:** [T89 — Run the split critic for one round](https://github.com/jerridan/crew/blob/main/docs/tickets.md#t89--run-the-split-critic-for-one-round)\n**Type:** Refactor\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n- `docs/design.md` §15.150 (new): the decision and its figures. It closes the open question that §15.148 left on the split critic.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/full-path.md`, \"Have the split reviewed\": owns the one-round rule, the no-report rule and the resume case for the split critic.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/record-format.md` owns the `reviews/` names.\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `skills/project-lead/references/full-path.md`: \"Have the split reviewed\" states one critic round per split. The project lead applies every accepted finding to `split.md`, blocking ones included, writes one `decisions.md` entry titled `Split critic <deliverable-id> r<n>: adjudication`, and the split goes to dispatch, with no second round, no cap and no question. A critic with no report is dispatched at the next reserved number. A resume adjudicates a report on disk and dispatches no critic. A re-plan gets its own one round.\n- `skills/project-lead/SKILL.md`: the label table's `blocking` row names the project lead's own edit of `split.md` for a split critic finding.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/record-format.md`: `<n>` of a split critic report counts the deliverable's critic rounds, one per split; `-r2` and `-r3` for one split in older records stay valid.\n- `agents/split-critic.md`: says no second round follows and the project lead fixes each accepted finding. Both verdict strings stay.\n- `skills/project-lead/scripts/crew-stats.py`: one comment; no code change.\n- `docs/design.md`: new §15.150; §15.148 and §15.118 point to it.\n- `docs/tickets.md`: new T89.\n- `CLAUDE.md`: Build state names T89.\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`: version 0.1.117.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\n- Version rule: the change touches `skills/` and `agents/`, so both manifests go to 0.1.117. The orchestrator assigned the numbers by merge order: the plan review PR takes 0.1.116 and §15.149.\n- One rule, one file: `full-path.md` owns the split critic's rules; `SKILL.md`'s spec critic paragraph speaks only of the spec critic.\n- Small edits in `full-path.md`, because another change edits the path files.\n- The verdict strings stay, because `crew-stats.py` and old records read them.\n\n### How this was verified\n\n- `grep -n -i -E 'three re-splits is the cap|dispatch again' skills/project-lead/references/full-path.md` prints nothing.\n- `grep re-split skills/project-lead/SKILL.md` prints nothing.\n- `python3 -m py_compile skills/project-lead/scripts/crew-stats.py` passes, and its diff is a comment.\n- A read of each changed file against the spec's seven requirements, with PR 171's diff as the pattern.\n\n### Known gaps\n\n- No run has used the one-round rule for the split critic yet. The round 2 sample is small (6 counted reports); the user accepted it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZgYWHHNhRSy3s6RFPj\n",
